<!--
  App-owned strings (not part of the auto-generated i18n translation_* catalog).

  The web TemplateGallery (web/src/features/dashboard/components/TemplateGallery.tsx) renders every
  template title/description/chrome string via t('templates.…', '<English fallback>') — e.g.
  t('templates.title', 'Dashboard Templates'), t('templates.default.desc', '…'). Those `templates.*`
  keys do NOT exist in the web react-i18next catalog (web/src/i18n/{en,ar,he}.json), so the web app
  renders the i18next *fallback* string in every locale. The neutral P1/S10 catalog (apps/shared/i18n,
  generated into the translation_* resources) therefore has no matching key to bind, and that catalog
  is auto-generated — it must never be hand-edited.

  To keep the native surface free of hardcoded English while reproducing the web verbatim, those strings
  live here as app-owned resources, mirroring the established preset_gallery_strings / nav_strings /
  auth_strings pattern. They are English-only in values/ on purpose: Android falls back to values/ for
  ar/he, which reproduces the web's missing-key fallback (English shown in every locale) exactly. The
  "Back" button reuses the real catalog key translation_common_back (it exists), and the widget count
  reuses the web "{{count}} widgets" plural-agnostic phrasing as a %1$s format string.

  template_gallery_empty has no web counterpart: the web data is a static non-empty constant, so the web
  never renders an empty gallery. It backs the native lifecycle "empty" state (a host feed could resolve
  to zero templates) so the surface is never a blank box.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="template_gallery_title">Dashboard Templates</string>
    <string name="template_gallery_detail">Template Preview</string>
    <string name="template_gallery_blank">Blank Dashboard</string>
